  "result": "I changed the project limit check in `src/server/services/project-service.ts` so it refuses the create that would put an organization over its limit. I haven't run the test suite, so the fix is untested.\n\n`createProject` called `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)`, which asks whether the organization is already over its limit rather than whether one more project would push it over. An organization at its limit passed the check, so the extra project got created. Only the next attempt was blocked. I changed the last argument from `0` to `1`.\n\nI did not touch the separate check in `create-project.ts`. It compares `projectsUsed >= limits.projects` and was already correct.\n\nI also noticed a mismatch I left alone. The comment in `create-project.ts` says archived projects should count toward the quota. But `recomputeUsage` skips archived projects, and `countProjects` skips them by default. If billing expects archived projects to count, that is a separate change.",
